WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.680
In this video, you add a second network interface to a running virtual machine. SUSE Virtualization plugs it in without a restart.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:13.380
The virtual machine is running. Open its action menu,

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.220
and select Edit Config.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:19.010
Open the Networks tab.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:26.550
The virtual machine has one interface, on the management network. You cannot change it while the machine runs.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:29.190
Select Add Network.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:33.480
Choose the VLAN network for the new interface.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:39.630
Keep the bridge type and the virtio model. Hot-plugging works with bridge interfaces.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:42.060
Select Save.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:50.010
SUSE Virtualization offers to restart the virtual machine. A new network interface does not need a restart.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:55.240
Select Save, not Save and Restart.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:58.990
Open the virtual machine's Networks tab.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:06.670
The virtual machine never stopped, and it now has a second interface on the VLAN network.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:13.649
You added a network interface without downtime. Next, you set up a dedicated network for live migration.
